    "notes": "Replace bracketed prompts with concise customer language. Keep each block to two or three lines.\nThe pitch: Identify the product category if it will help the audience understand the offer.\nCustomer and problem: Name a specific user, buyer, buying trigger, and current alternative. Quantify the cost of the problem where possible.\nSolution: Explain the customer workflow and the mechanism that produces the benefit.\nValue proposition: State one primary measurable outcome, timeframe, meaningful comparison, and reason to believe.\nEvidence: Cite the source, date, sample size, and baseline for any result. Distinguish tested results from assumptions. If no evidence exists, state the hypothesis and how you will validate it.\nOffer and next step: Specify the pricing unit, one clear action, owner or contact, deadline, and success measure."
